+
+### Selector context projection (S6 live-01 realization correction)
+
+The selector's full FramedSynthesisTask remains its authoritative input and exact
+input digest; raw response binding and dynamic reference domains are unchanged.
+The existing owned assembly presents a pure judgment projection rather than
+serializing that complete execution carrier. Original task/source/case meaning
+is present once in readable text, alongside the current oracle and worksite
+contents. An exact source text already inside the original task is located there
+within the same prompt; only an identical source block is omitted from repeated
+work-order instructions. Purpose, outcome, read/write/check scope, fixed testing
+commands and assessment subject/rubric remain explicit.
+
+Active obligation meaning, selected completeness/depth/strength rules, discovery
+classes, coverage gaps and current/historical evidence remain visible. Integrity
+carriers, schema asset bytes, duplicated source bindings and complete command
+execution envelopes remain in bound input, not model context. The projection
+keeps actual command streams/status, native reports, assessment findings, Result
+refs, byte-currentness facts and the current prior judgment without reconstructing
+history or semantically choosing relevant work. The 131072-byte case bound still
+applies. A bounded-context refusal retains its already-computed structured cause
+through the existing preparation exception boundary. The affected discriminator
+is the real baseline fold → parent reevaluation → next task → owned assembly,
+plus unchanged dynamic-domain/raw-answer and exact input identity checks.
